that the left can't actually win in fighting it&nbsp;
on an issue by issue basis. And I'll explain why.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:02.320 --> 00:01:06.960
But it's also a culture war that the right has&nbsp;
no interest in winning. That's a really important&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:06.960 --> 00:01:12.080
thing to understand, because the right benefits&nbsp;
from it being an ongoing war as a strategy to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:12.080 --> 00:01:17.680
justify people donating money to them and voting&nbsp;
for them in elections because you need them to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:22.880
continue fighting the war. If they win the war,&nbsp;
then it's over. The entire impetus for saying&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:23.440 --> 00:01:28.000
these are the reasons you need to donate to us.&nbsp;
And here's why we don't actually talk about policy&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.720
goes away if they win so they can never&nbsp;
actually win for their own self-preservation.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:33.360 --> 00:01:38.080
There's a really interesting article from about&nbsp;
two or three months ago in Politico magazine&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:38.080 --> 00:01:45.200
called How the Culture War Could Break Democracy.&nbsp;
Zack Stanton wrote it. And in the article, Zack&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:45.200 --> 00:01:50.560
references James Davis and Hunter, sociologist&nbsp;
from the University of Virginia, who years ago&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:51.120 --> 00:01:58.640
described culture war as cultural flashpoints&nbsp;
with political ramifications. And that's a really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:01:58.640 --> 00:02:05.200
good definition. These are flashpoints, meaning&nbsp;
places, events or times when trouble, violence&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:05.200 --> 00:02:11.360
or anger flare up flash points on the basis of&nbsp;
cultural disagreements. But they're not just&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:12.640 --> 00:02:17.600
irrelevant cultural disagreements. They have&nbsp;
political significance in a very real way.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:18.400 --> 00:02:23.760
Think through some examples. The so-called debate&nbsp;
over critical race theory is actually a really&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:23.760 --> 00:02:28.480
good example of this. This is a flashpoint&nbsp;
that is really a cultural issue. What is the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:34.480
culture in schools that the left versus the&nbsp;
right wants? What's the culture of workplaces&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:41.680
when it comes to race and an understanding of race&nbsp;
that is generating disagreement and unrest? And&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:41.680 --> 00:02:46.480
it's politically significant in that Republicans&nbsp;
and the right are weaponized it to justify people&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:46.480 --> 00:02:53.120
voting for them instead of voting for Democrats&nbsp;
perfect culture war, for example. Now, why do I&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:59.040
say it's not apparent to me that the culture war&nbsp;
is winnable? And I want to be really careful in&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:02:59.040 --> 00:03:04.720
how I explain this. As far as the American right&nbsp;
wing's right wing goes, Republicans don't have a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:04.720 --> 00:03:10.960
plan to win the culture war because the winning&nbsp;
is to continue fighting the culture war forever.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:10.960 --> 00:03:16.800
As I mentioned earlier, all of these cultural&nbsp;
issues, even when they subside in real life,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:16.800 --> 00:03:22.080
the right keeps talking about them as if they&nbsp;
are real problems. The entire war on Christmas&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:22.080 --> 00:03:28.960
is a very good example of this. That was always&nbsp;
merely a cultural issue and it was being laid on&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:28.960 --> 00:03:35.680
top of ideas of nationalism, freedom of religion,&nbsp;
alleged hostility from the left against religion,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:35.680 --> 00:03:41.280
patriotism, and even after the subject of&nbsp;
whether we say Merry Christmas or Happy Holidays&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:41.280 --> 00:03:44.960
essentially disappeared completely, like at some&nbsp;
point it just went away. It wasn't even a thing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:45.520 --> 00:03:51.760
Republicans continued to act as though the&nbsp;
very same war on Christmas continued to take&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:51.760 --> 00:03:56.000
place almost as an aside, like, of course. Yeah.&nbsp;
We're also still fighting the war on Christmas,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:03:56.000 --> 00:04:01.040
even though it wasn't actually an issue in&nbsp;
society. So the point is Republicans don't&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:01.040 --> 00:04:05.680
plan to actually win the culture war because they&nbsp;
benefit by fighting it, whether they win it or&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:05.680 --> 00:04:10.080
they lose it or they have the majority public&nbsp;
opinion on their side or against their side,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:10.080 --> 00:04:15.920
they will continue to claim that the culture wars&nbsp;
going on and that it must be fought and they are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:15.920 --> 00:04:19.760
the people to fight it. So you'd better donate&nbsp;
to them and vote for them so they can fight it&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:19.760 --> 00:04:24.880
for you. That's what's happening right now with&nbsp;
socialism and communism. I mean, look at these&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:24.880 --> 00:04:31.120
last six months of Joe Biden, Joe Biden's first&nbsp;
six months in office. It's become very clear Joe&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:31.120 --> 00:04:36.160
Biden is not a communist. Joe Biden is not a&nbsp;
socialist. Joe Biden is not a Marxist. Now,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:36.160 --> 00:04:40.240
if you'd been paying attention for the last four&nbsp;
decades, you would know that about Joe Biden.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:40.800 --> 00:04:47.200
But now that Joe Biden is president and he's done&nbsp;
no socialist stuff, he's done no communist stuff,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:48.160 --> 00:04:53.600
have the discussions about Biden's communism&nbsp;
and socialism gone away from the right? No,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:54.240 --> 00:04:59.840
because for Republicans, especially in the&nbsp;
absence of any policy. And in particular,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:04:59.840 --> 00:05:06.800
especially when the country is increasingly not&nbsp;
with Republicans on policy, they need to have some&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:06.800 --> 00:05:12.880
war to point to. So now they point to we've got to&nbsp;
fight communism and socialism. Trump did it at his&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:12.880 --> 00:05:18.080
speech, his rally in Phenix on Saturday, which we&nbsp;
covered yesterday. So Republicans have no plan to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:18.080 --> 00:05:22.400
win the culture war. That's a feature, not a bug.&nbsp;
All right, fine. But what about the left? What&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:22.400 --> 00:05:27.360
about Democrats? What about progressives? However&nbsp;
you define that movement? The unfortunate thing.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:28.480 --> 00:05:34.320
Is that these cultural issues aren't actually&nbsp;
won by fighting them directly, and there's a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:34.320 --> 00:05:39.840
couple of reasons for that. And I think a perfect&nbsp;
example to understand this is abortion rights.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:39.840 --> 00:05:46.000
Abortion rights is an issue that the right has&nbsp;
fought in two ways. The right has fought against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:46.000 --> 00:05:52.320
abortion rights as a cultural issue in churches&nbsp;
and through colloquial rhetoric. But the right&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:52.320 --> 00:05:59.840
has also fought abortion rights as a legal issue&nbsp;
ever since we saw Roe v. Wade legalized abortion&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:05:59.840 --> 00:06:05.920
in most cases decades ago. We've seen Republicans&nbsp;
fight abortion rights at the state level in a&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:05.920 --> 00:06:11.920
legal sense, and then they've also fought it as&nbsp;
a cultural issue on television and as an issue.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:11.920 --> 00:06:17.680
We must preserve life and humanity. Even the term&nbsp;
pro-life is a propaganda term you use when you are&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:17.680 --> 00:06:22.880
fighting this as a cultural issue, you're framing&nbsp;
anybody who doesn't share your view is against&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:22.880 --> 00:06:28.800
life. There is no coincidence about the right&nbsp;
choosing the term pro-life for their position.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:28.800 --> 00:06:36.400
And the American right has essentially lost the&nbsp;
abortion fight in in a legal sense. What I mean by&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:36.400 --> 00:06:42.480
that and in a cultural sense, what I mean by that&nbsp;
is while some states have successfully curtailed&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:42.480 --> 00:06:48.640
abortion rights with state level restrictions,&nbsp;
it's still a fight in that sense that still is&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:48.640 --> 00:06:53.040
being legislated in the courts. But we have&nbsp;
a situation today in twenty twenty one where&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:53.040 --> 00:06:58.160
the country is more in favor of abortion&nbsp;
being legal in most cases than at any time&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:06:58.160 --> 00:07:02.720
in the last 40 years. Republicans have been&nbsp;
fighting abortion for 40 years or even longer,&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:02.720 --> 00:07:07.760
and the country is more in favor of abortion being&nbsp;
legal in most cases today than at any previous&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:07.760 --> 00:07:13.680
point. It's an abject failure by Republicans,&nbsp;
by the right to fight against abortion rights.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:18.240
But that's not because Democrats go around talking&nbsp;
about how great abortion is, and that's one of the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:18.240 --> 00:07:23.760
complexities of fighting the culture war because&nbsp;
of the way that the right frames these issues.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:23.760 --> 00:07:28.880
And they do a good job of it. I have to give them&nbsp;
credit. The left is put in a position where if you&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:28.880 --> 00:07:35.040
fight them directly head on on the issue,&nbsp;
you get framed as, oh, well, so you want more&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:35.040 --> 00:07:39.200
abortions. And then all of a sudden now you're&nbsp;
fighting against that and it becomes a mess.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:39.760 --> 00:07:48.160
But then here's the other thing. Bigger picture.&nbsp;
The culture in the US has shifted and as a result&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:48.160 --> 00:07:53.920
of that, issues like income inequality and&nbsp;
the environment have taken more center stage&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:07:54.480 --> 00:08:02.640
and opposition to abortion has just faded. So&nbsp;
a lot of the reason that the soft opposition to&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:02.640 --> 00:08:07.600
abortion has gone away isn't because of Democrats&nbsp;
going around and saying abortion is great.&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:08.160 --> 00:08:13.040
It's because a lot of people realized, yeah, we&nbsp;
actually don't even really need to be talking&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:13.040 --> 00:08:17.600
about that. We need to be talking about income&nbsp;
inequality and access to health care and the&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:17.600 --> 00:08:24.320
damage we're doing to the environment, etc. It's&nbsp;
not a fight that makes sense. And so with a lot of&nbsp;&nbsp;

00:08:24.320 --> 00:08:29.520
these things, I don't know that there's anything&nbsp;
to win by fighting issues head on. I'll think&nbsp;&nbsp;

